[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3533189516","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112761#issuecomment-3533189516","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112761","id":3533189516,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SmDGM","user":{"login":"Benjamin-Dobell","id":482276,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MjI3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/482276?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell","html_url":"https://github.com/Benjamin-Dobell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T15:03:53Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T15:03:53Z","body":"I probably should note that I mentioned the digital on/off values are mapped to 0 and 1 analog values. However, the code implemented is using -1.0 for the off state. That's because an axis will typically operate in the range [-1, 1]. The code that maps triggers (specifically) to the range [0, 1] is [part of Godot's core input handling](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/input/input.cpp#L1417-L1420).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3533189516/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587783190","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112761#issuecomment-3587783190","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112761","id":3587783190,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V2ToW","user":{"login":"Benjamin-Dobell","id":482276,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MjI3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/482276?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell","html_url":"https://github.com/Benjamin-Dobell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-28T03:15:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-28T03:19:17Z","body":"@Alex2782, I appreciate you taking a look at this PR. However, I'm not quite sure I understand your comment. Are you able to elaborate?\r\n\r\nThis PR relates to making digital buttons emulate analogue triggers. It's one layer lower-level than the device mappings. The OS has built-in support for L1, L2, R1, R2 etc. Now that L2/R2 digital buttons are handled, you can then proceed to remap the corresponding analogue axis in the mapping files if desired i.e. we can't remap `KeyEvent.KEYCODE_BUTTON_L2` to anything unless we're handling it, which prior to this PR, we weren't. Godot itself doesn't support digital L2/R2 buttons, so they can't come through to the mapping file as digital buttons.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587783190/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3588867478","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112761#issuecomment-3588867478","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112761","id":3588867478,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V6cWW","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-28T11:01:38Z","updated_at":"2025-11-28T11:01:38Z","body":"Okay, I'll test this PR on my gamepads first. Which gamepads did you test on exactly, name/`GUID`?\r\n\r\nTry this demo:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/misc/joypads","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3588867478/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3599283563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112761#issuecomment-3599283563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112761","id":3599283563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WiLVr","user":{"login":"Benjamin-Dobell","id":482276,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MjI3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/482276?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell","html_url":"https://github.com/Benjamin-Dobell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Benjamin-Dobell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-01T22:46:58Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T22:47:18Z","body":"Bugger. That's unexpected. I don't have a Series X controller, unfortunately. Sorry about that! I generally like to own my PRs fully and not push work onto maintainers where possible. But yeah, in this case I don't own the necessary hardware 😅\r\n\r\nI do have some Xbox One (original) and Xbox 360 controllers (with wireless receiver) in some cupboards somewhere. I'll pull those out tonight and at least give those a go.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3599283563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3599347521","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112761#issuecomment-3599347521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112761","id":3599347521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Wia9B","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-01T23:06:14Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T23:06:14Z","body":"> I probably should note that I mentioned the digital on/off values are mapped to 0 and 1 analog values. However, the code implemented is using -1.0 for the off state. That's because an axis will typically operate in the range [-1, 1]. The code that maps triggers (specifically) to the range [0, 1] is [part of Godot's core input handling](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/input/input.cpp#L1417-L1420).\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112761#pullrequestreview-3517200506\r\n\r\nI think it can also be configured, therefore I believe that some changes on the Android side in the Java file are not necessary, or could lead to regressions on some gamepads. \r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f5918a9d35350bf6402dd1b4902ab539747d77a6/core/input/godotcontrollerdb.txt#L7-L9\r\n\r\n\r\n`lefttrigger:+a4,righttrigger:+a5` \r\n\r\nBack then, I only had to insert a `+` sign here to solve a problem where the L/R triggers were stuck at 0.5. And maybe we can swap the buttons here so they're correct. I probably didn't test properly, always pressing both triggers simultaneously 😃 \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f5918a9d35350bf6402dd1b4902ab539747d77a6/core/input/input.cpp#L1723-L1747\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3599347521/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3599416318","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112761#issuecomment-3599416318","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112761","id":3599416318,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Wirv-","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-01T23:27:25Z","updated_at":"2025-12-02T00:06:20Z","body":"> Bugger. That's unexpected. I don't have a Series X controller, unfortunately. Sorry about that! I generally like to own my PRs fully and not push work onto maintainers where possible. But yeah, in this case I don't own the necessary hardware 😅\r\n> \r\n> I do have some Xbox One (original) and Xbox 360 controllers (with wireless receiver) in some cupboards somewhere. I'll pull those out tonight and at least give those a go.\r\n\r\n\r\nThat's no problem, please also include the gamepad name and GUID. You can copy it in the Godot Editor if you're testing the public demo project.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"768\" height=\"137\" alt=\"Bildschirmfoto 2025-12-02 um 00 16 46\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/26f04b79-2a61-4d88-bd5c-05cedb3d444f\" />\r\n\r\n---------------\r\n\r\nWhen I submitted a PR with a bug fix a few months ago, I asked the community for more testers with an Xbox gamepad. Two more people responded, and we all had this gamepad with this GUID. In the `gamecontrollerdb.txt` file, I discovered more Xbox gamepads and copied them as well, adding a \"+\" sign to each one (`lefttrigger:+a4,righttrigger:+a5`). A Google search for `Xbox One Controller` showed this gamepad looked very similar (I think the only thing missing was the Share button), so I'm hoping the L/R triggers will work identically.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f5918a9d35350bf6402dd1b4902ab539747d77a6/core/input/godotcontrollerdb.txt#L7-L20\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3599416318/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]